WEBVTT

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.070
Too sweet!

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.420
My, such manners!

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.300
H-hey, it was too sweet for me...

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.570
At times like this,
you’re supposed to say,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.080
“Dango taste worlds different when

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.710
I’m with a cute maiko like you.”

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.190
Don’t call yourself cute.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.730
I know, but you could at
least say that to be polite!

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.720
I hate telling lies.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.250
It’s a LIE?

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.260
N-nah, it’s not really
a lie, I guess...

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.240
Wh-what now?

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.270
It’s nothing.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.460
But dang, you’ve got it rough.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.090
You have practice during the day

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.310
and then spend the night
dealing with drunks.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.590
It would be unbearable
if all of my patrons

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:55.190
were like Serizawa-han.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.140
You can be surprisingly blunt.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.780
Yep!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.020
Oh, yeah!

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.340
Shimabara is going to
be quiet for a bit.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.020
Why is that?

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.970
Serizawa-san will be going to Osaka

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.750
in a couple of days due to work.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.570
Osaka?

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.260
Yeah. I’m going with him.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.260
Shimabara may be okay,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.450
but I’m worried he might torment

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.940
the maiko and geisha in Osaka...

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.010
I’ll make sure that Serizawa-san

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.770
doesn’t get rough with them.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.550
Really? I will hold you to that!

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.300
O-okay...

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.460
You can count on me!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.140
Thank you for the treat. Later!

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.290
Yeah! See ya!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.500
Y-Yamazaki?!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.510
The Light of a Flashing Sword

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.590
You didn’t come all
the way from the east

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.170
just to flirt with a geisha, did you?

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.270
Huh? Well...

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.920
Keep your flippant behavior in check!

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.130
I can’t stand your half-assed stance.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.410
If you’re one of us, join us!

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.030
If you’re leaving, go!

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.130
Why don’t you make up your mind?

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.740
It’s not like I’m staying
there because I want to!

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.220
Serizawa-san--

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.730
You always blame things on Serizawa-san!

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.790
Bluntly put, you can’t act
on your own volition, can you?

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.050
What was that?!

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.260
When you get down to it, you are merely

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.120
using Serizawa-san as an excuse.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.990
You’re nothing more than a pet dog

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.050
that can’t survive on its own!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.380
You lack loyalty to the Roshigumi,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.560
which has provided you a home.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:12.060
An disloyal pet dog is
inferior to a stray.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.210
I don’t have to put up
with you calling me a dog!

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:20.740
And besides, you guys are
just behind the times,

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.280
pretending to be samurai when

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.910
you weren’t even born
into the warrior class!

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.870
Behind the times?!

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.950
You bastard!

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.960
Why you--!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.470
I was born into the family
of an acupuncturist.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.380
But I was desperate to become a samurai,

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.470
so I pretended to be a
ronin in Kyoto and Osaka.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.380
Yet I felt that the more I
tried to outwardly copy them,

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.340
the further I drew from the
true essence of a samurai.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.450
When I joined the Roshigumi,

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.340
Hijikata-san said that everyone
would be treated like warriors

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.990
regardless of their upbringing.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.290
I thought that I could
become a samurai here.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.250
Note: Kakae-ire referred to those who had been
promoted to Gokenin, a shogunal vassal.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:19.250
My father was originally a
kakae-ire ranked samurai.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.380
You were born into the warrior class?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.070
But Dad was hard up for money,
so he sold the family armor

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.160
and ultimately died leaving
behind nothing but debt.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.610
I did some pretty degrading work

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.620
while putting up with my mother...

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.500
...wailing about how I was
a “shameful samurai.”

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.610
If I didn’t work,

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.650
we wouldn’t be able
to buy food the next day.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.080
Even so, just the fact that you carry

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.790
samurai blood makes me envious.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:54.160
Sannan-san, what is going
to happen to Ryunosuke?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:55.770
Meaning what?

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.390
He’s a... good guy.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.500
He’s super honest.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.920
Really, he shouldn’t
be in a place like this!

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.500
I understand what you are
getting at, Toudou-kun.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.010
But you see, he has learned
too much about us.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.930
Osaka

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.130
Well then, Serizawa-san,

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:20.810
we have other errands to attend to,

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:21.940
so if you’ll pardon us.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.130
Yeah, that’s fine.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.760
Nagakura-kun, I take it
you will accompany me.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.720
M-me?

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.450
Well...

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.090
Good luck!

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:38.580
H-hey!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.000
That one is two shuban.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.030
The one with the picture is one ryou.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.660
Then I’ll take this one.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:51.720
Thank you.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:53.970
Hey!

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.720
Serizawa-san said he’s
goin’ out drinkin’.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.730
So, like, Ryunosuke, you’ll
join us, won’t you?

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.530
I’m worried he might torment

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.730
the maiko and geisha in Osaka...

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.750
I’ll make sure he doesn’t
get rough with them.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.740
Really? I will hold you to that!

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.600
Sure, I’ll go.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.740
Huh? For real?

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.250
Whoa, dude! What’s gotten into him?

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.250
What are you doing?!

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.250
Sir?

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.610
If you want to please your customers,

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:33.760
unwind your obi, remove
your full kimono and dance!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.760
S-Serizawa-san?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.300
We couldn’t possibly!

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.130
We are geisha, so we sell our--

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.270
Silence!

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:48.210
How dare lowly women from the

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.210
red-light district reject an order

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.660
from Kamo Serizawa,
Chief of the Roshigumi!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.000
Serizawa-san!

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.440
You’ve had too much to drink!

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.450
I will not tolerate such insult!

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:06.170
Summon your master!

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.270
Ryunosuke!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:07.940
Yeah!

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.530
Go get Kondou-san and Hijikata-san!

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.820
I-I’m on it!

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.180
I am terribly sorry.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.860
We were in the wrong.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.550
Please forgive us!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.190
I will give them a harsh
scolding, so please!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.650
Please forgive them!

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.350
Why don’t we let them off
with that, Serizawa-san?

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:30.440
Hijikata-san!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.260
If they were men, I would
behead them over this,

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.420
but since they are women,

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.680
I will merely chop off
their hair instead.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.680
You’ll what?!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.830
Serizawa-san!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.920
If you do that, we wouldn’t be able

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.830
to entertain from tomorrow on.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.340
You have but your own foolishness

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.840
for insulting a warrior to blame.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.400
Hold it, Serizawa-san!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.800
You’re the one who insulted them
first by telling them to strip!

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:54.800
Silence!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:57.620
Ibuki!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.750
Serizawa-san!

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.010
Wasn’t this supposed to be a party?

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:02.770
There is no need to get so livid!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:06.020
Cur, you do it.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.530
That is your punishment
for opposing your master.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.030
To-to hell with that...!

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:20.030
Th-there’s no way...
I could ever do that!

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.340
That right?

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.170
Then I’ll do it.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.440
But since I’m drunk,

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:32.050
I might inadvertently cut of their
heads instead of their hair.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.050
Have mercy!

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.550
Stop!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.550
Then will you offer
me your head instead?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:47.220
You’ll be satisfied if we sever
their chignons, Serizawa-san?

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.060
Toshi!

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.680
I’ll do it.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.850
Hijikata-san!

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.080
Toshi!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.140
Very well. This should make for
some nice entertainment.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.500
P-please forgive me!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.590
Hijikata-san!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.360
I truly regret what
I said, so please...!

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:16.090
Don’t move.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.100
Please forgive me! Please forgive me!

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.980
Please forgive me!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.920
Please forgive me!

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.040
Several Days Later,
Kyoto

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.550
Ryunosuke!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.180
Word of that incident in
Osaka has reached here.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.070
We came to protect Kyoto,

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:53.560
but what’s the point
when the locals hate us?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.000
The Roshigumi is not about popularity.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.720
What we must do is stay true
to our squad’s mission.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.080
I know that, but...

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.200
Whining won’t get us
nowhere. Let’s go.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.100
S-sure...

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.730
What is Hijikata-san up to?

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.210
The commander is busy,

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:19.220
having personally suggested the
Osaka-Kyoto

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:20.740
joint sumo demonstration.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:23.820
I knew he was one of them!

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.620
He’s buddies with the Wolves of Mibu.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.130
They behaved brutally in Osaka!

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:36.800
What will they do next?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.650
I wish they’d leave Kyoto!

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.180
Kosuzu, we’re going.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:51.890
Come along.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.290
Serizawa-san!

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.790
You... You...!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.200
You go on about warrior pride and

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.670
yet you soil that very pride!

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.430
Why are you so upset?

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.550
A lowly cur dares to
speak of warrior pride?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.180
What a joke.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.480
Going to draw?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:36.060
You DO know what
that means, do you not?

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:43.070
There is no need to hold back. Draw.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:47.990
What’s keeping you?

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:51.080
Aren’t you prepared to die?

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.580
Can’t draw? I’m hardly surprised.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.900
I... I...!

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:05.450
I imagine that after getting the
cold shoulder from the locals

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.470
the girl you love dumped you.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.180
With nowhere to vent your rage,

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.010
you came to take it out on me.

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:14.750
Does that sound about right?

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:20.210
Of course, there is no way you
could form the resolve to die.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.740
After all, you cannot even
form the resolve to live.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:25.740
What?!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.180
What will you dedicate your life to?

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.950
It is impossible for someone
who can’t even decide that

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.710
to form the resolve
to die for something.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:40.650
I picked up a life that was about
to expire on a mountain road,

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:44.280
but in the end, it was of no real value.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.060
You are unable to decide
how to spend your life.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.470
It is ludicrous for a lowly cur

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.770
living in peace to speak
of pride and resolve!

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.520
Serizawa-sensei, is
something the matter?

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:59.440
Ibuki, what are you doing?!

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:02.710
What has gotten into him?

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.460
Serizawa-sensei...?

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.790
That sobered me up.
I’m going out to drink.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:22.570
Is that a souvenir for
that little maiko?

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.990
Couldn’t give it to her?

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:32.300
Ryunosuke, just how serious are you?

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:36.960
I’m not sure, but I care for her...

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.060
Until now, I’ve never felt...

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.560
...this way for someone.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:44.130
That girl works in the
red-light district.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.420
Even if you wanted to
start a family with her,

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.320
it would cost a fortune
to buy her freedom.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.840
If you’re resigned
to remain her patron,

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.080
you’ll have to turn a blind eye
to her pleasing other men.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:59.020
Either way, it will take a fair amount
of resolve on your part.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.550
Resolve...

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.170
Half-hearted sentiment and
actions will ultimately...

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:08.230
...just make that young lady cry.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.950
Is it true that Saiki is under arrest?

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:17.730
Yeah. Supposedly Serizawa-san is
questioning him right now.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.940
Using Serizawa-sensei’s name to

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.480
take various loans is a hefty crime.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.830
When you combine that with
how you stole his pouch

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.490
and pawned it off to repay them...

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.390
You have strayed from
the way of the warrior!

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.490
Commit honorable suicide.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.310
P-please forgive me!

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:41.440
Never again... I will
never do that ever again!

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.730
Please! Please!

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.000
Then I will give you a choice.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.010
A... choice?

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.510
Slice open your gut or
drink this medicine.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:53.370
M-medicine?

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.600
Isn’t that the Water of Life?

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.020
Right. I have refined it.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.230
There is a chance you may
survive if you drink it.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.340
What do you say?

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.460
I-I’ll drink it!

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.330
I’ll take that medicine
or anything you like!

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.980
I just don’t want
to slice myself open!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.530
Serizawa-san, shouldn’t we wait until

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.290
after we have consulted with
Kondou-san and Hijikata-kun?

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:18.160
That is unnecessary.
This decision belongs to Saiki alone.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.430
Power is welling up inside of me!

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:36.700
He hasn’t lost his sanity even
though he has become a fury!

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.430
It-it worked!

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:51.590
I don’t want to die!

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:54.940
I don’t want to die!

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:57.950
Damn it...!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.660
Is it true that the medicine worked?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.640
Whatever the case, Saiki
ultimately became a fury.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:04.960
We have to find him!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.460
H-help me...

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:14.090
Is someone there?

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.470
Aren’t you... Saiki-san?!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.180
Fellow corps member Sasaki

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:29.150
was killed at Suzakuno
Senpon Way with a woman.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:33.110
We believe the culprit was Saiki,
who has turned into a fury.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.610
Got any proof?

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:39.260
The locals are talking about how
they heard animal-like growls.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:42.620
Furthermore, there was hardly any
blood left in the corpses.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.610
He drank their blood?
That’s messed up!

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.630
Supposedly Sasaki died trying
to defend the young lady.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:52.740
He protected his woman, didn’t he?

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.180
Until the very end...

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:59.190
We must find Saiki has soon
as possible and kill him.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:00.610
I would you like you to split up

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.310
and begin searching for him right away.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.600
Nagakura-kun, Harada-kun,
search Shimogyou.

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:05.550
’Kay!

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:06.680
You got it.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:09.150
Toudou-kun, Inoue-san, search Nakagyou.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:12.150
Okita-kun, please search Kawaramachi.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:16.050
Isn’t the Choshu Domain’s
mansion in Kawaramachi?

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:18.410
You want me goin’
somewhere that dangerous?

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.910
I’m asking you to go precisely
because it is dangerous.

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:24.890
Very well, then.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.730
If you find the fury, please
be sure to kill him!

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.350
But of course.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.660
Saiki is in Shimabara?

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:40.680
Correct.

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:43.180
I am certain it was him.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:46.210
Aren’t Kondou-san and
the others out at Gionsha?

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:48.900
They’re at the sumo demo
that’s being held as a sign of gratitude.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:49.990
Got it.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.620
A fury in Shimabara?

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:58.180
Kosuzu!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.180
Need somethin’?

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.230
I’m going. He’s in Shimabara, right?

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.190
Deadweight.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:08.600
You’ll get in my way if I

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.710
gotta protect you while fighting a fury.

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.230
I don’t plan on asking
for your protection.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.090
I’m going of my own accord.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:17.920
If you think I’m in the
way, just cut me down.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:25.190
You’re over there, aren’t you?

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:30.050
You smell just like the last fury that
fled from our headquarters.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.930
Blood! Give me blood!

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.580
Forget it.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.540
I missed?!

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:53.380
Okita!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:07.760
Souji!

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.130
Don’t let anyone near here.

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:14.130
Right!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:16.650
Well done.

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.690
It’s not like I did this to earn

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.650
a compliment from you, Hijikata-san.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.120
Why did you come?

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.170
I bet you just got in his way.

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:26.450
Well...

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:30.660
He wasn’t a complete
and total deadweight.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.230
Sorry, but please stay back!

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.720
I’m heading on back.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:34.870
Keep back!

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:37.720
You’re a moron.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.990
’Scuse me for being stupid.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:41.950
Go back and rest.
You did a job well done.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.030
Sannan-san, you wanted me

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.260
to kill that fury, didn’t you?

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.750
What would make you think that?

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:00.260
You sent me to the most
dangerous location

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:03.090
and deliberately pushed that I
was to kill him, remember?

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.410
It’s because you have aptitude.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.700
Aptitude?

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.340
Indeed. Aptitude to be our “sword.”

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:15.620
Okita, you must become
the Roshigumi’s sword.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.670
The Roshigumi’s sword?

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:21.900
The rogue samurai fear
Souji Okita’s sword

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.720
and are awe-struck by the Roshigumi.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.720
Henceforth, I imagine your sword will
get drenched in far more blood.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:32.870
Even if it goes against the desires
of our chief, Kondou-san,

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:34.730
show no mercy as you cut men down.

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:28.870
There was no need to set the place

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:30.600
ablaze if you lacked hard evidence!

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:33.050
That man really is a nuisance.

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:36.660
I am well aware that I will
writhe in agony as I die.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.390
Hmph. Lowly human.

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.400
The Brightly Burning Beacon
